<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cowal</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cowal is a peninsula in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argyll">Argyll</a> and Bute in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, between Loch Fyne and the Firth of Clyde, with Dunoon as its main town. In the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was the land of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cenel-comgaill">Cenél Comgaill</a>, one of the kindreds of the Gaelic kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dal-riata">Dál Riata</a>, whose name the peninsula preserves.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cowal.jpg" alt="Cowal" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Photograph: NASA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cowal_peninsula_landsat.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
